<Base title="Will Quantum Computers Break Bitcoin? Timeline and Fix - OpenBitcoin" description="Can quantum computers break bitcoin, and when? The honest timeline of 2035 to 2045 at the earliest, which coins are exposed, and the BIP-360 fix.">
<main class="wrap doc-wrap">
  <div class="doc-head">
    <div class="doc-kicker">Learn · Security</div>
    <h1>Will quantum computers crack bitcoin?</h1>
    <p class="doc-lede">Quantum computers will eventually derive a bitcoin private key from an exposed public key, but not today, not this decade, and not by surprise. Here is when, which coins are at risk, and the fix.</p>
    <div class="doc-updated">Learn · Security · updated July 2026</div>
  </div>
  <div class="doc-grid">
  <div>
    <div class="qt-verdict">
      <span class="qt-vdot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <p><b>The short version:</b> no quantum computer in existence can touch bitcoin today, and the latest expert survey puts roughly one-in-three odds on a cryptographically relevant machine within a decade, likely within fifteen years. The cryptography community already has standardized quantum-resistant signatures, Bitcoin has an upgrade path being actively designed, and the network would see a real attack coming years in advance. Nothing needs to happen to your coins this decade, but the work to protect the next one has already started.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="qt-stats">
      <div class="qt-stat"><div class="qt-sv">1,200 to 1,450<em>logical qubits</em></div><div class="qt-sk">needed to break a bitcoin key</div></div>
      <div class="qt-stat"><div class="qt-sv">&lt;100<em>logical qubits</em></div><div class="qt-sk">best machines today</div></div>
      <div class="qt-stat"><div class="qt-sv">~4M<em>BTC</em></div><div class="qt-sk">in quantum-exposed outputs</div></div>
      <div class="qt-stat"><div class="qt-sv">2024<em>done</em></div><div class="qt-sk">NIST post-quantum standards</div></div>
